From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:10:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 07/17] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: fix saving and
 restoring the TX power control index

When TX power control is disabled, its current gain index is saved so
that re-enabling it can start from there. Two bugs:

- The whole status register was saved. The index is in bits 8-14; the
  low byte holds the estimated output power. The saved value was almost
  always above B43_PHY_HT_TXPCTL_CMD_C1_INIT, so it was never restored.
- Restoring wrote the index to the command registers with a plain
  write. For core 1 that is TXPCTL_CMD_C1, which also holds the enable
  bits set just before: power control would be switched off again.

Currently power control is only toggled once, during init, right after
a PHY reset, when nothing has been saved yet; the bugs would show as
soon as it is disabled and re-enabled around anything else.

Fixes: 418e8b680516 ("b43: HT-PHY: store TX power state before disabling it")
Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
index b259fefc3826..cca3a5ebd8e5 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
@@ -546,10 +546,14 @@ static void b43_phy_ht_tx_power_ctl(struct b43_wldev *dev, bool enable)
 
 	if (!enable) {
 		if (b43_phy_read(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TXPCTL_CMD_C1) & en_bits) {
-			/* We disable enabled TX pwr ctl, save it's state */
+			/* We disable enabled TX pwr ctl, save its state.
+			 * The status registers hold the current gain index
+			 * in bits 8-14; the low byte is the power estimate.
+			 */
 			for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
 				phy_ht->tx_pwr_idx[i] =
-					b43_phy_read(dev, status_regs[i]);
+					(b43_phy_read(dev, status_regs[i]) >> 8) &
+					B43_PHY_HT_TXPCTL_CMD_C1_INIT;
 		}
 		b43_phy_mask(dev, B43_PHY_HT_TXPCTL_CMD_C1, 0xffff & ~en_bits);
 	} else {
@@ -560,11 +564,15 @@ static void b43_phy_ht_tx_power_ctl(struct b43_wldev *dev, bool enable)
 				b43_phy_write(dev, cmd_regs[i], 0x32);
 		}
 
+		/* Only replace the index field: a plain write would also
+		 * clear the enable bits in CMD_C1 set above.
+		 */
 		for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
 			if (phy_ht->tx_pwr_idx[i] <=
 			    B43_PHY_HT_TXPCTL_CMD_C1_INIT)
-				b43_phy_write(dev, cmd_regs[i],
-					      phy_ht->tx_pwr_idx[i]);
+				b43_phy_maskset(dev, cmd_regs[i],
+						~B43_PHY_HT_TXPCTL_CMD_C1_INIT,
+						phy_ht->tx_pwr_idx[i]);
 	}
 
 	phy_ht->tx_pwr_ctl = enable;
